{"id":18,"word":"Courtship","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"કૉર્ટશિપ","english_meaning":"The period of time during which a couple develop a romantic relationship before marriage.","gujarati_meaning":"પ્રણય-ગાળો — લગ્ન પહેલાં પ્રેમ-સંબંધ વિકસાવવાનો સમય.","synonyms":["wooing","dating","romance"],"antonyms":["separation","divorce"],"collocations":["long courtship","traditional courtship","courtship rituals"],"word_forms":["courtships","court"],"usage_note":"Old-fashioned but still used; 'dating' is the modern equivalent.","memory_tip":"'Court' = રાજ-દરબારમાં પ્રભાવ — courtship = પ્રેમ જીતવાનો પ્રયાસ.","examples":["Their courtship lasted three years before marriage.","Traditional courtship involved family involvement.","He wrote letters during their courtship.","Their courtship began at a college festival."]},
{"id":19,"word":"Engagement","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"એન્ગેજ્મેન્ટ","english_meaning":"A formal agreement to marry; the period between proposal and marriage.","gujarati_meaning":"સગાઈ — લગ્ન માટેની ઔપચારિક સ્વીકૃતિ અને પ્રતિજ્ઞા.","synonyms":["betrothal","promise of marriage"],"antonyms":["breakup"],"collocations":["engagement ring","engagement party","announce engagement"],"word_forms":["engagements","engaged","engage"],"usage_note":"'Engaged' is the adjective ('We are engaged'). An 'engagement ring' is given at the proposal.","memory_tip":"'Engage' = જોડવું → engagement = બે જ઼િંદગી જોડવાની ઘોષણા.","examples":["They announced their engagement at a family dinner.","Her engagement ring is a beautiful diamond.","The engagement party was held at a hotel.","They had a two-year engagement before marrying."]},
{"id":20,"word":"Proposal","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"પ્રોપોઝ઼ل","english_meaning":"An offer of marriage made to someone.","gujarati_meaning":"લગ્ન માટે ઔપચારિક પ્રસ્તાવ — 'શું તમે મારી સાથે લગ્ન કરશો?' એ ક્ષણ.","synonyms":["marriage offer","proposition"],"antonyms":["rejection"],"collocations":["marriage proposal","romantic proposal","proposal accepted"],"word_forms":["proposals","propose","proposed"],"usage_note":"'Pop the question' is an informal expression for making a proposal.","memory_tip":"'Propose' = આગળ મૂકવું → proposal = લગ્ન માટે આગ્રહ.","examples":["He made a romantic proposal on the rooftop.","She accepted his proposal with tears of joy.","The proposal surprised everyone in the family.","He planned the proposal for months."]},
{"id":21,"word":"Betrothal","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Less common","gujarati_pronunciation":"બિટ્રૉધ-ઓ઼-ľ","english_meaning":"A formal agreement to marry; an engagement.","gujarati_meaning":"સગાઈ-કરાર — લગ્ન માટે ઔપચારિક પ્રતિજ્ઞા.","synonyms":["engagement","promise of marriage","pledge"],"antonyms":["dissolution","called off"],"collocations":["betrothal ceremony","formal betrothal","betrothal agreement"],"word_forms":["betroth","betrothed"],"usage_note":"Formal/literary term; in everyday speech 'engagement' is used.","memory_tip":"'Be-troth' → 'troth' = pledge (જૂની અંગ્રેજીમાં) → betrothal = પ્રતિજ્ઞા-બદ્ધ.","examples":["The betrothal ceremony was grand and traditional.","Their betrothal was announced at the family gathering.","She was betrothed at a young age.","The betrothal lasted two years before the wedding."]},
{"id":22,"word":"Affection","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"અફ઼ૅક્શન","english_meaning":"A gentle feeling of fondness or liking for someone.","gujarati_meaning":"પ્રેમ-ભાવ/સ્નેહ — કોઈ પ્રત્યે હળવી, ઊષ્મ-ભરી લાગણી.","synonyms":["fondness","love","warmth","tenderness"],"antonyms":["coldness","indifference","hatred"],"collocations":["show affection","deep affection","terms of affection"],"word_forms":["affectionate","affectionately"],"usage_note":"'Affectionate' is the adjective; 'affection' is milder than 'love'.","memory_tip":"'Affect' = અસર → affection = હૃદય પર અસર = સ્નેહ.","examples":["She showed great affection toward her grandchildren.","He greeted his old friend with genuine affection.","Children need affection and attention to thrive.","Their affection for each other was obvious."]},
{"id":23,"word":"Devotion","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ડિવોશન","english_meaning":"Strong love, loyalty, or commitment to a person or cause.","gujarati_meaning":"સમર્પણ — ઊંડો પ્રેમ, વફ઼ાદારી; સ્વ-ભૂલીને અન્ય માટે જીવવું.","synonyms":["dedication","loyalty","commitment","love"],"antonyms":["neglect","disloyalty","indifference"],"collocations":["show devotion","devotion to family","lifelong devotion"],"word_forms":["devoted","devote","devotedly"],"usage_note":"Used for both religious and personal relationships.","memory_tip":"'Devote' = સમર્પિત → devotion = પ્રેમ-સ-ભ-ઉ-ભ = સ-ઉ-ભ = સ.","examples":["Her devotion to her family is admirable.","He showed his devotion by being there every day.","Their marriage was built on love and devotion.","Religious devotion brought the couple closer."]},
{"id":24,"word":"Infatuation","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ઇન્ફ઼ૅચ્યૂએશન","english_meaning":"An intense but short-lived passion or admiration for someone.","gujarati_meaning":"ઘેલ/ક્ષણિક પ્રેમ — કોઈ પ્રત્યે તીવ્ર પણ ટૂંક-ગ઼ाળ-ની ભ્રામક પ્રેમ-ભાવ.","synonyms":["crush","obsession","puppy love"],"antonyms":["indifference","hatred"],"collocations":["teenage infatuation","mere infatuation","infatuation fades"],"word_forms":["infatuate","infatuated"],"usage_note":"Distinct from true love; infatuation is intense but temporary.","memory_tip":"'Infat' sounds like 'infant' — infatuation = baby-love, not deep mature love.","examples":["His infatuation with her faded after a few months.","She mistook infatuation for love.","Infatuation is common in teenage years.","What started as infatuation turned into lasting love."]},
{"id":25,"word":"Compatibility","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"કૉમ્પૅટિબિલિટી","english_meaning":"The ability of two people to exist and work together harmoniously.","gujarati_meaning":"અનુકૂળતા — બે વ્યક્તિઓ વચ્ચે સ્વભાવ, મૂલ્ય અને જીવન-શૈલીની સુસંગતતા.","synonyms":["harmony","agreement","suitability"],"antonyms":["incompatibility","mismatch"],"collocations":["relationship compatibility","test compatibility","compatibility issues"],"word_forms":["compatible","incompatible","compatibly"],"usage_note":"Used in both romantic and professional contexts.","memory_tip":"'Compat' (together) → compatibility = સાથે ચાલી શકવાની ક્ષ઼મતા.","examples":["They checked their compatibility before marriage.","Compatibility is key to a happy marriage.","The couple had great emotional compatibility.","Astrology is often used to check compatibility in India."]},
{"id":26,"word":"Reconciliation","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"રિકૉન્સિલિએશન","english_meaning":"The process of making two people friendly again after a disagreement or separation.","gujarati_meaning":"સમાધાન — ઝઘડા કે ભૂલ પછી ફરીથી મૈત્રી/સ્નેહ સ્થાપવાની પ્રક્રિયા.","synonyms":["resolution","settlement","reunion","making up"],"antonyms":["estrangement","conflict"],"collocations":["seek reconciliation","marital reconciliation","path to reconciliation"],"word_forms":["reconcile","reconciled","reconciliatory"],"usage_note":"Often used in both romantic and political contexts.","memory_tip":"'Re' (again) + 'concile' (harmony) → reconciliation = ફ઼ રી-મ-ઐ-ત્-ર-ી = ફ઼ ર઼ ી-સ-ન-ě-હ.","examples":["After months apart, their reconciliation was emotional.","Couples therapy helped their reconciliation.","The family reunion led to reconciliation among siblings.","He made the first step toward reconciliation."]},
